id: pm-vcs-p7bisect
title: Bisect stable changes using a linked pm test command
description: "Add pm vcs bisect driven by pm test <id> --run, persisting change-id results across history rewrites and restoring the original working state."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-18T03:01:48.622Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-20T01:47:10.558Z"
author: codex-agent
estimated_minutes: 480
acceptance_criteria: Good/bad boundaries identify the first failing stable change using the linked real pm test; rewritten commit ids reuse change results; interrupted/failed tests and conflicted candidates have explicit outcomes; TOON and JSON report the result and original state is restored.
parent: pm-vcs-phase7
dependencies[1]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
  pm-vcs-p7objects,blocked_by,"2026-10-18T03:01:58.591Z",codex-agent,"cli:update:dep",detected
comments[34]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-19T12:32:18.951Z",pi-agent,"Plan for bisect: single command 'pm vcs bisect' with start|good|bad|skip|run|status|reset subcommands. Durable session state lives in the worktree's private control directory (atomic write) so a crash mid-walk leaves a resumable session; session milestones (start, conclusion, reset) are appended to PM history as comments on the linked item, so concurrent agents see each other's sessions and append-only history is never clobbered. Candidates are ordered oldest-first by ancestry; outcomes are keyed by stable change identity so rewritten commit ids (rebase/amend/describe) reuse recorded results. Linked test execution reuses the pm SDK runTest (pm test --run semantics). Outcomes: good, bad, skip (manual), untestable (spawn/timeout/signal/empty), conflicted (candidate carries unresolved conflict units). Original branch and commit are restored after success, refusal, SIGINT and crash-resume."
  "2026-10-19T13:15:08.442Z",codex-agent,"Resuming the interrupted implementation as codex-agent. Reviewing durable state, linked-test semantics, restore safety, candidate ordering and cross-agent history before completing real-repository proofs and unchanged release gates. Existing uncommitted work is preserved."
  "2026-10-19T13:24:41.877Z",codex-agent,"Review fixes: execute each candidate in a disposable native repository so tracked PM history and original checkout bytes survive test side effects, SIGINT and SIGKILL. Rebased results now map stable identities to current ancestry. Exit 125 is skip; unresolved potential culprits produce ambiguous rather than a false first_bad. Per-worktree process leases prevent concurrent local mutation; separate linked instances append start/step/halt/done/reset receipts to the shared tracker. The annotate refactor shares immutable historical harness/model provenance with the bisect report."
  "2026-10-19T13:33:56.892Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: disabling only selectBisectCandidate (returning no candidate) made both the 64-change history and rewritten-history regressions fail (0 passed, 2 failed). Restored the production function immediately. Added explicit candidate-log budget/omission reporting because the pinned PM host rejects universal read-output controls for the mixed bisect command. Long comments must be verified through full item reads; the SDK comments response abbreviates them. Public-data demo uses a locally trusted linked test, not a command inherited from a foreign Git ref."
  "2026-10-19T13:39:21.833Z",codex-agent,"Public-data proof completed: imported 34 committed public pm-csv tracker snapshots, spanning source revisions 53807ddccac4d5190deebdb52661ec398a44d0ed through 417072bd7c402f5f8d3387beb37b33d8c887ab6b. A real linked PM test identified the deliberately introduced regression at snapshot 18 (source fad7e30c040dff33f789bd6c5176882b27825427) in four executions; original checkout verified at the bad tip. Reproducer: test/bisect-demo.ts; complete TOON receipt: docs/bisect-demo.toon. Seven focused safety/CLI/legacy/budget tests pass, including SIGKILL during an active test, worker ownership refusal, unauthorized-worker refusal and resume. Annotation provenance retains its original caches; the 2000-change bounded-read regression passes."
  "2026-10-19T13:40:44.889Z",codex-agent,"The recorded linked test was executed through the pinned PM CLI with --run --only-index 1 --timeout 900 --progress: 26 tests passed, zero failed/skipped/cancelled. Full read-only annotation checks also pass, including the bounded 2000-change read proof. Core tracker authority passes with extensions disabled; normal health separately flags a pre-existing pm-github host-version skew. No dependency pins or append-only history were repaired or rewritten."
  "2026-10-19T13:56:31.357Z",codex-agent,"The full gate exposed packaging coupling: native consumers configured with **/*.toon correctly interpret every installed .toon file as a PM item, so a TOON-format report cannot use that extension. Renamed the unchanged public demo receipt to docs/bisect-demo.txt and updated its documentation link; no parser rules or tests were weakened. Reproducing both existing packed-consumer regressions after the rename."
  "2026-10-19T14:05:51.439Z",codex-agent,"Both packed-consumer regressions pass after renaming the raw TOON receipt as text (2 passed, 0 failed). The full-source inventory guard also requires its explicit expected count to increase from 67 to 70 for engine/bisect.ts, bisect-commands.ts and bisect-test-runner.ts. Updated only that count; all production globs, ignore-directive prohibition and per-file 100 percent coverage thresholds remain intact."
  "2026-10-19T14:50:13.738Z",codex-agent,"Final acceptance: npm run release:check and bun run release:check each passed 1,695/1,695 tests, zero failed/skipped/cancelled/todo. All 70 production files have per-file 100 percent statements, branches, functions and lines at unchanged thresholds (24,576 lines/statements and 848 functions; npm 7,662 branches, Bun 7,661). Both full gates used isolated HOME/Git configuration and verified copies of the indexed implementation. Final fixture-counter isolation passed the complete focused suite: 28/28. Direct installed Bun CLI bisect also found the known culprit in two linked-test executions and preserved the original checkout. Public demo: 34 distinct real tracker trees, four executions, known snapshot 18; behavioral revert: two expected regression failures. Only the PM acceptance receipt and claim-release record remain to be committed with a regenerated self-host archive. Item remains nonterminal for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-19T15:28:57.136Z",codex-agent,"Review round 1: verified the root-parent crash, HEAD manual-default mismatch, reset milestone ordering, and repeated ancestry reads. Plan: cover each behavior with revert-sensitive regressions, cache range-bounded ancestry and immutable commit reads per walk, compact report ids with --full recovery, measure demo bytes, run both release gates at unchanged coverage thresholds, refresh the self-host archive, and push without resolving review threads."
  "2026-10-19T15:34:20.409Z",codex-agent,"Round 1 regressions: root commits in unrelated merged history retain explicit and file-derived item links; all three manual outcomes target next while HEAD stays fixed; exhausted walks refuse with an explicit-revision remedy; reset removes state/workspaces before attempting its milestone and returns a warning if the item disappeared. Range decisions share cached ancestry. Scaling proof: 2,000 commits, 1,600 candidates, 2,000 setup commit reads, 10 decisions, zero additional commit reads per decision or final verdict (materialization excluded). Public demo still identifies snapshot 18 in four executions; captured TOON report shrank from 2,834 to 1,516 bytes (1,318 bytes, 46.5 percent). Default ids are 12 characters; --full retains full ids; redundant boundary revision/detail text is omitted. Six new focused regressions passed before behavioral revert checks."
  "2026-10-19T15:35:32.009Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral reverts verified independently against review head 13d39a3: linkedItems (root-parent failure), registerBisectCommands (manual HEAD mismatch, absent-candidate remedy missing, reset item-not-found failure), reportOf (64-character ids instead of 12), and each of bisectCandidates, bisectRemaining, selectBisectCandidate, bisectVerdict (read bounds exceeded). All nine targeted revert runs failed as expected; functions restored immediately after each run. The range-construction revert exceeded 2,000 reads at read 2,001; each decision-function revert exceeded the zero-additional-read bound on its first read. No review threads changed."
  "2026-10-19T15:37:34.360Z",codex-agent,"Restored implementation acceptance: pinned pm test --run --only-index 1 --timeout 900 --progress passed the complete focused suite, 34/34 tests, zero failures/skips/cancellations/todo. Typecheck, build, test compilation, lint, zero-duplication and docstring checks pass. Core tracker health and validation pass with extensions disabled. Preparing the committed source and self-host snapshot for both full release gates under isolated HOME and Git configuration."
  "2026-10-19T16:47:30.738Z",codex-agent,"Release acceptance update: npm run release:check passed all 1,701 tests and every downstream gate. Bun passed 1,701 tests, all 70 production files at per-file 100 percent statements/branches/functions/lines, native TOON, stat-cache, committed self-host equality, audit, identities and packing, then correctly refused changelog verification because its verification clone was shallow. This is a clone setup error, not a package defect. Fetching complete history and tags, checking the affected tail gates, and rerunning the unmodified full Bun command. Implementation CI is green on Node 22 and 26, both Windows launcher jobs and CodeQL; no source or threshold changes are needed."
  "2026-10-19T17:23:31.423Z",codex-agent,"Final round 1 acceptance on implementation 0ff4504: npm run release:check and the full-history bun run release:check both exited zero, each with 1,701/1,701 tests and zero failed/skipped/cancelled/todo. All 70 production files have per-file 100 percent statements, branches, functions and lines at unchanged thresholds: 24,650 statements/lines, 858 functions, 7,716 branches in both final runs. Both commands passed native TOON, installed-CLI stat-cache tracing, committed self-host equality, production audit, identity audit, packaging, changelog and release attestations under isolated HOME/Git configuration. The earlier shallow-clone setup failure is corrected; the complete Bun command was rerun successfully after fetching full history and tags. Focused pinned pm linked-test run passed 34/34. Nine independent behavioral revert cases fail as expected; the final root-parent assertion was rechecked and rejects the undefined object id. Scaling: 2,000 commits, 1,600 candidates, exactly 2,000 setup commit reads and zero decision/verdict reads across 10 decisions; materialization is outside that bound. Demo: 34 public trees, four executions, snapshot 18, 2,834 to 1,516 TOON bytes (46.5 percent smaller). Fresh-clone core health and validation pass. Implementation CI is green for Node 22/26, both Windows launcher jobs and CodeQL. No new PM CLI defect or UX gap was encountered. Releasing the claim without closing the feature; final receipt and self-host snapshot will be committed and pushed, with final-head CI status recorded on PR 131. No review threads were replied to or resolved and no merge was performed."
  "2026-10-19T19:26:59.846Z",codex-agent,"Review round 2: fetched every review thread and all comments; two unresolved Major findings remain (PRRT_kwDOToJT7M6uEUgB and PRRT_kwDOToJT7M6uEUgP). Latest CodeRabbit review has no Outside diff range findings. Both issues are valid in engine/bisect.ts. Plan: constrain unresolved verdicts to the first bad candidate ancestry, cover both sibling byte orders and skipped ancestors through direct verdict and runBisect, and copy only the selected tree closure with an object-count regression. Remote head is current and contains origin/main (zero behind), so no merge or reconcile is needed. Will record independent behavioral reverts, run both unchanged release gates with isolated Git identity, regenerate the self-host archive, and push without changing review threads."
  "2026-10-19T19:28:23.796Z",codex-agent,"Independent behavioral revert proofs completed against review head a2d1a0e, rebuilding after each revert. Reverting only bisectVerdict caused the sibling regression to fail (ambiguous instead of first_bad; 0 passed, 1 failed). Reverting only runBisect candidate object collection (and its required reachable import) caused the materialization regression to fail (24 copied objects instead of 4 at depth 12; 0 passed, 1 failed). Both production fixes were restored immediately and rebuilt. Fixed regressions pass 2/2: sibling order permutations retain skipped ancestors; 12-commit history copies 12 objects across 3 candidates, 64-commit history copies 20 across 5 candidates, exactly four objects per candidate with correct clean nested-file contents, original checkout preservation and scratch cleanup. No wall-time assertions."
  "2026-10-19T19:29:28.231Z",codex-agent,"Restored implementation passed the pinned PM linked-test run: 2/2 regressions, zero failed/skipped/cancelled/todo. Both findings have independent failing revert proofs recorded above. Preparing the committed implementation and current self-host archive for full npm and Bun release gates; coverage thresholds and dependency pins are unchanged."
  "2026-10-19T20:14:55.052Z",codex-agent,"Final round 2 release acceptance on implementation f8fb53b: npm run release:check and bun run release:check both exited zero, each with 1,703/1,703 tests and zero failed/skipped/cancelled/todo. All 70 production files reached per-file 100 percent statements, branches, functions and lines at unchanged thresholds: 24,651 statements/lines, 858 functions and 7,722 branches in both runs. Both complete gates passed native TOON, installed-CLI stat-cache strace acceptance, committed self-host equality, production audit, identity audit, packaging, changelog and release attestations under isolated HOME/Git configuration; Bun used an independent full-history no-local clone. Fresh-clone core health and validation have no blocking errors, with the same pre-existing tracker advisories as at orientation. Implementation CI is green on Linux Node 22/26, both Windows launcher jobs and CodeQL; skipped review apps are not fresh review approval. Both valid Major threads are fixed and independently revert-proven: the verdict revert yields ambiguous instead of first_bad; the materialization revert copies 24 objects instead of 4. Fixed object counts are 12 objects for 3 candidates at depth 12 and 20 for 5 at depth 64, with correct clean materializations and unchanged source checkout. The linked regression command passed 2/2 through the pinned PM CLI. No new PM CLI bug or UX gap was encountered. Releasing the claim without closing the feature. The final receipt changes only tracker evidence and the self-host archive; TypeScript source remains byte-identical to the fully tested implementation, and final-head archive/health/CI checks will be verified. No review threads were replied to or resolved, and no merge or release was performed."
  "2026-10-19T21:12:07.245Z",codex-agent,"Review round 3: all unresolved threads and all their comments fetched (no pagination gaps). PRRT_kwDOToJT7M6uGOgc and PRRT_kwDOToJT7M6uGOgp are valid: shallow ancestry walks read absent parents, and deterministic checkout errors leave retry-only pending candidates. Latest CodeRabbit review contains no Outside diff range findings. Remote PR head is current and zero commits behind main; no merge or reconcile needed. Plan: real shallow-clone and denied-payload regressions, independent behavioral reverts, both unchanged full release gates under isolated Git identity, current self-host snapshot, and push without thread replies/resolution. Initial merge-fence drift was checked during npm ci installation; history remains append-only."
  "2026-10-19T21:13:45.415Z",codex-agent,"Independent behavioral revert proofs against head 1d4f362: restoring only boundaryAncestry plus bisectCandidates makes the real depth-two merge clone regression fail with object_not_found for an omitted parent (0 passed, 1 failed). Restoring only runBisect makes the real denied-payload checkout regression throw object_not_found instead of finishing with an explicit untestable observation (0 passed, 1 failed). Each revert was rebuilt, tested independently, and immediately restored. Fixed regressions pass 3/3: both shallow merge parents retained without hydration; denied checkout recorded exactly once, durable before progress, ambiguous conclusion, no test execution or retry; unexpected checkout and typed runner errors retain pending/retry semantics, original checkout and scratch cleanup verified."
  "2026-10-19T22:37:35.475Z",codex-agent,"npm run release:check completed successfully on implementation e1d5b2800115050dd98539a99686b9ae6cfe05ff under isolated HOME/Git configuration: 1706/1706 tests, zero failed/skipped/cancelled/todo. All 70 production files have per-file 100 percent statements, branches, functions and lines at unchanged thresholds: 24658 statements/lines, 858 functions, 7730 branches. Native TOON, real stat-cache tracing, committed self-host equality, production audit, identity audit, packaging, changelog and release attestations all passed. Implementation CI is also green on Linux Node 22/26, both Windows launcher jobs and CodeQL. Bun continues in an independent full-history clone. Separately reproduced a shallow-culprit provenance-report failure with a real SDK tracker and native depth-two merge clone: start succeeds; manual bad and status both read an omitted parent and fail. Deduplication found no existing specific issue; follow-up pm-vcs-bisect-shallow-report is open under this feature. That reporting path is outside the two requested review threads; no additional production change was made during gate execution."
  "2026-10-19T22:41:07.269Z",codex-agent,"Final review round 3 acceptance on e1d5b2800115050dd98539a99686b9ae6cfe05ff: npm run release:check and bun run release:check both exited zero, each with 1706/1706 tests and zero failed/skipped/cancelled/todo. Both full commands used isolated HOME/Git configuration; Bun used an independent full-history no-local clone. All 70 production files reached per-file 100 percent statements, branches, functions and lines at unchanged thresholds: 24658 statements/lines and 858 functions in both runs; npm 7730 branches, Bun 7731. Both complete commands passed native TOON, real installed-CLI stat-cache tracing, committed self-host equality, production and identity audits, packaging, changelog and release attestations. The pinned PM linked regression command passed 3/3, and both independent behavioral reverts failed as recorded above. Implementation CI is green on Linux Node 22/26, both Windows launcher jobs and CodeQL; skipped automated rereviews are not new review approval. Core health and validation passed from a fresh no-local clone with existing advisories. Open follow-up pm-vcs-bisect-shallow-report records the separately reproduced omitted-parent provenance-report bug; it is not part of the two requested review threads. No new PM CLI bug or UX gap was found. Releasing the claim without closing the feature. The final receipt contains tracker evidence and a refreshed self-host snapshot; TypeScript source remains identical to the fully tested implementation. Final-head snapshot/health/CI verification will be recorded on PR 131. No review threads were replied to or resolved, and no PR merge or software release was performed."
  "2026-10-19T23:22:53.784Z",codex-agent,"PR 131 review round: both unresolved threads are valid (PRRT_kwDOToJT7M6uIuUq shallow culprit reporting; PRRT_kwDOToJT7M6uIuU4 worker stdin errors). Latest review has no outside-diff findings. Remote head is current and contains main. Add real shallow-clone and early-exit regressions, prove each by reverting its changed function in memory, self-review related paths, then run both unchanged release gates and verify pushed CI."
  "2026-10-19T23:25:29.104Z",codex-agent,"All three regressions passed (3/3). Behavioural revert proofs replaced only linkedItems, runCandidateTest, or traceFile with the remote-head function, rebuilt dist, and ran its focused test: each exited 1. linkedItems: manual shallow bad returned object_not_found. runCandidateTest: real early-exit worker caused uncaught write EPIPE in its parent subprocess. traceFile: omitted shallow ancestor caused object_not_found. Restored functions and rebuilt. Self-review found the same unguarded first-parent read in traceFile; shallow non-root deltas are now omitted, later changes and true roots remain. Bisect reports expose itemsBoundary=shallow and retain sorted unique explicit associations. No history rewriting or stashing used."
  "2026-10-19T23:25:53.418Z",codex-agent,"Focused regressions also passed through the pinned pm linked-test runner (3 tests, zero failures). Source policy checks passed. Local health now passes after installing the same project extension version as CI; no merge receipts are pending. Existing stale-item and legacy provenance advisories remain untouched. Next validation is the full npm and Bun release gate under an isolated Git identity, with unchanged per-file 100 percent coverage thresholds."
  "2026-10-19T23:42:38.377Z",codex-agent,"Gate progress: npm has passed the new regressions and the existing atomic-publication race test. The concurrent Bun gate reported one failure in the unchanged test review atomic publication preserves native permission failures and known orphan owner metadata. The same test passed independently in the acceptance clone (1/1, zero skipped/cancelled/todo). Awaiting its full-run assertion detail, then repeat the complete Bun gate serially without changing assertions, timing or thresholds. No failure has appeared in the changed bisect or attribution paths."
  "2026-10-20T00:03:19.557Z",codex-agent,"npm run release:check exited 0 on implementation 4b343545339046f8da1c9a92378e8f765e026bce with isolated HOME and Git configuration: 1709/1709 tests, zero failed/cancelled/skipped/todo. All 70 production files reached unchanged per-file 100 percent statements, branches, functions and lines (24668 statements/lines, 858 functions, 7746 branches). Native TOON, installed-CLI stat-cache tracing, committed self-host equality, production audit, physical Git identity audit, package dry run, changelog and both release attestations passed. The independent Bun retry remains in progress without failures; it passed the exact unchanged composition test that failed in the first attempt. The earlier failure was confirmed as the existing erasure-control metadata inspection class and is documented with a deterministic synthetic orphan-PID repro on pm-vcs-simi. Because that repro is data-dependent, the unchanged retry runs in its independent clone while npm acceptance completes; this revises the earlier serial-retry plan without changing any test or threshold."
  "2026-10-20T00:22:29.172Z",codex-agent,"Final review-round acceptance on implementation 4b343545339046f8da1c9a92378e8f765e026bce: npm run release:check and bun run release:check both exited 0, each with 1709/1709 tests and zero failed/cancelled/skipped/todo. Both used isolated HOME and Git configuration; Bun ran in an independent no-local full-history clone. All 70 production files reached per-file 100 percent statements, branches, functions and lines at unchanged thresholds: 24668 statements/lines and 858 functions in each; npm 7746 branches, Bun 7745. Both complete commands passed native TOON, installed-CLI stat-cache tracing, committed self-host equality, production and identity audits, packaging, changelog and release attestations. The three new regressions passed through the pinned PM runner (3/3), and their independently reverted functions each failed as recorded. The dedicated shallow-issue command also passed 1/1 through pinned PM. Test-result tracking is disabled, so results are retained in comments without changing policy. Both unresolved findings were valid; latest review had no outside-diff findings. Self-review additionally fixed traceFile shallow-parent access. The first Bun attempt was stopped after a pre-existing uninspectable_payload refusal; an unchanged complete retry passed, without remediating the separately documented pm-vcs-simi orphan-metadata defect. The final receipt changes only tracker evidence and selfhost.bundle; code, tests, docs, pins, workflows and thresholds remain identical to the tested implementation. Releasing claims without closing items. Exact final-head clone health, validation, self-host and CI will be verified before stopping. No review threads were replied to or resolved; no merge or software release occurred."
  "2026-10-20T00:26:18.747Z",codex-agent,"Main advanced during acceptance with Dependabot commit 1f275320f82a734c088284707680702c682efc19, changing only eslint 10.12.0 to 10.13.0 in package.json and package-lock.json. Merged origin/main normally as e02e516cccd658b417703f751d463c6270dafb56, reinstalled the lockfile, and passed npm run lint plus bun run lint with the updated ESLint. Post-merge strict health passed with no pending merge receipts; only the existing stale-item and legacy-provenance advisories remain. Production TypeScript, tests, docs and workflows are byte-identical to full-gated implementation 4b343545339046f8da1c9a92378e8f765e026bce. The complete 1709/1709 npm and Bun gate results above are same-source acceptance before the lint-only dependency refresh; the affected updated-tool gate was rerun, and exact final-head CI will validate the integrated dependency set. Package manifests are explicitly excluded by the self-host policy. Refreshing the archive for this tracker receipt, releasing the claim without closing, and verifying the final head before stopping."
  "2026-10-20T01:16:25.816Z",codex-agent,"Review round for PR #131: refreshed the remote branch; origin/main is already an ancestor. Fetched all review threads and complete comments (no pagination remaining). The only unresolved thread is PRRT_kwDOToJT7M6uKJjW: manual non-good outcomes on the good boundary are accepted but ignored by range-based decisions. Verified valid; will reject those outcomes with a restart remedy, clarify the boundary contract, cover engine and CLI behavior, and prove the regression by reverting only markBisectOutcome. Latest CodeRabbit review has no Outside diff range findings. No review replies or resolutions will be posted."
  "2026-10-20T01:17:49.551Z",codex-agent,"PRRT_kwDOToJT7M6uKJjW fixed: markBisectOutcome resolves the current good boundary once and rejects every non-good outcome before appending a step. The error directs reset/start with an earlier good revision; docs distinguish the excluded good boundary from the correctable bad boundary. Independent behavioral revert against 83fa9bd: replaced only markBisectOutcome with its old implementation, rebuilt, then ran node --expose-gc --test --test-name-pattern=\"manual (engine|CLI) verdicts\" test/bisect.test.ts. Both regressions failed (0 passed, 2 failed): missing expected engine exception and absent CLI refusal. Restored the function and rebuilt immediately; pinned pm test --run --only-last --timeout 900 --progress passed 2/2 with zero failed/skipped/cancelled/todo. Tests cover bad/skip/untestable/conflicted rejection, accepted good and candidate outcomes, outside-range validation, unchanged durable state/PM comments/checkout after refusals, readable status, and correction of the bad boundary to no_bad_change. Whole PR diff self-review checked boundary declaration, candidate filtering, stable-id verdict lookup, manual/default mark paths, run completion, reporting and provenance changes for ignored accepted verdicts; no further instance found in the current mutation paths. Typecheck, build, test compilation, lint, zero duplication and docstrings pass. No thresholds or dependency pins changed."
  "2026-10-20T01:45:49.787Z",codex-agent,"npm run release:check passed in full on e11b709f4b2bb9d6dc89957a0e3ec77dbd900105 with isolated HOME/Git configuration: 1711/1711 tests, zero failed/cancelled/skipped/todo. All 70 production files reached per-file 100 percent statements/branches/functions/lines at unchanged thresholds: 24673 statements/lines, 858 functions, 7749 branches. Native TOON, real installed-CLI stat-cache strace acceptance, committed self-host equality, production audit, identity audit, packaging, changelog and release attestations all passed. Bun continues in an independent full-history no-local clone. Exact implementation-head CI passed Linux Node 22/26, both Windows launcher jobs and CodeQL; skipped CodeRabbit/manual-review-required is not fresh review approval. Fresh-clone strict core health and validation have no blocking errors; existing tracker advisories remain. The fixed good-boundary regressions and their two failing function-level reverts are recorded above."
  "2026-10-20T01:47:09.950Z",codex-agent,"Final review-round acceptance on implementation e11b709f4b2bb9d6dc89957a0e3ec77dbd900105: npm run release:check and bun run release:check both exited zero, each with 1711/1711 tests and zero failed/cancelled/skipped/todo. Both complete gates used isolated HOME/Git configuration; Bun ran in an independent full-history no-local clone. All 70 production files reached per-file 100 percent statements/branches/functions/lines at unchanged thresholds: 24673 statements/lines and 858 functions in both runs; npm 7749 branches, Bun 7747. Both commands passed native TOON, real installed-CLI stat-cache strace acceptance, committed self-host equality, production and identity audits, packaging, changelog and release attestations. The pinned linked regression command passed 2/2; reverting only markBisectOutcome and rebuilding made both tests fail (0/2), then the function was restored and rebuilt. The final review fetch has complete threads/comments with no pagination gaps, still only PRRT_kwDOToJT7M6uKJjW unresolved, and no new Outside diff range findings. Remote main remains an ancestor. Implementation CI passed Linux Node 22/26, both Windows launcher jobs and CodeQL; skipped/manual-required reviewers are missing fresh review evidence. Existing tracker advisories and the separate pm-vcs-simi erasure follow-up remain outside this change; this round encountered no new PM CLI bug or UX gap. Releasing the claim without closing the item. The final receipt changes only tracker evidence and its self-host snapshot; source, tests, docs, dependency pins, workflows and thresholds remain identical to the fully gated implementation. Final-head archive, tracker integrity, changelog and identity checks will be verified before stopping. No review threads were replied to or resolved and no PR merge or software release was performed."
